#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:6
msgid "Unsafe External Functions"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:8
msgid ""
"You can declare foreign functions for access from Rust with `unsafe extern`. "
"This is unsafe because the compiler has no way to reason about their "
"behavior. Functions declared in an `extern` block must be marked as `safe` "
"or `unsafe`, depending on whether they have preconditions for safe use:"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:14
msgid "// Copyright 2025 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:15
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:19
msgid "\"C\""
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:20
msgid ""
"// `abs` doesn't deal with pointers and doesn't have any safety "
"requirements.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:23
msgid ""
"/// # Safety\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// `s` must be a pointer to a NUL-terminated C string which is valid "
"and\n"
"    /// not modified for the duration of this function call.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:31
msgid "\"Absolute value of -3 according to C: {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:34
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: We pass a pointer to a C string literal which is valid for\n"
"        // the duration of the program.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:36
msgid "\"String length: {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:36
msgid "\"String\""
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:43
msgid ""
"Rust used to consider all extern functions unsafe, but this changed in Rust "
"1.82 with `unsafe extern` blocks."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:45
msgid ""
"`abs` must be explicitly marked as `safe` because it is an external function "
"(FFI). Calling external functions is only a problem when those functions do "
"things with pointers which might violate Rust's memory model, but in general "
"any C function might have undefined behaviour under any arbitrary "
"circumstances."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:50
msgid ""
"The `\"C\"` in this example is the ABI; [other ABIs are available too]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/items/external-blocks.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md:52
msgid ""
"Note that there is no verification that the Rust function signature matches "
"that of the function definition -- that's up to you!"
msgstr ""
